    stylePrompt: "Absurdist chamber pop / art-gallery performance piece, 92 BPM. Polite cello and viola ostinato, very serious. Espresso machine hiss sampled as hi-hat. Spoken-word verses over the quartet. Fog-release: strings detune slightly; a chorus of gallery guests hum one note wrong on purpose. End: everything snaps back to normal on a single polite clap. Intimate spoken female lead, Laurie Anderson gravity, never belted. Mood: pretentious until it is accidentally sincere, then collective denial. Use a dry close spoken voice (Justine-adjacent) with a polite quartet that refuses to smile.",
    lyrics: "[Intro — Ostinato]\n(Cello + viola, espresso hiss as hi-hat)\n\n[Verse 1 — Spoken]\nThe melon asks what you'll absorb tonight\nI absorbed the truth and the canapés\nThe tubes are honest. The fog is on time.\nArtforum says it's brave.\n\n[Chorus]\nThe melon asks\nWhat you'll absorb tonight\nI absorbed the truth\nAnd the canapés\nThe fog lifts\nAnd we pretend we're fine\nArtforum says\nIt's brave\n\n[Verse 2 — Spoken]\nNinety seconds of weather that tells the truth\nSomeone proposes. Someone files. Someone hates berries.\nMy watch says be present. I am. Unfortunately.\nJustine eats a cracker like a verdict.\n\n[Chorus]\nThe melon asks\nWhat you'll absorb tonight\nI absorbed the truth\nAnd the canapés\nThe fog lifts\nAnd we pretend we're fine\nArtforum says\nIt's brave\n\n[Bridge — Detuned]\n(Strings sag. Guests hum one note wrong.)\nI absorbed my ex-wife's lawyer. Does that count.\nThe melon does not answer. That is the installation.\n\n[Outro]\n(One polite clap. Quartet in tune again. Nobody makes eye contact.)",
