    stylePrompt: "Nocturnal electro-chanson at 84 BPM. Soft muted kick, sine bass, AM-bandwidth coloring kept musical, dashboard glow as the only bright practical, dark top end, tape hiss and a dead carrier as the bed — not live-station static. Radio Voice lead: intimate, slightly worn, never seen, never confirmed to be Continuity Voice, no belting, no pop vibrato. A second female close-mic (Rubella or Lillith, one sister only on the “live” line) sings the present-tense part. **Structural flaw:** the harmony / ghost double is always the other sister’s line from one bar ago — it answers late, with last bar’s words, every phrase, the entire runtime. Do not align the stack. Do not “correct” the delay in the final chorus. Mood: wrong-reflection carpool; the station closed in 1998 and is still in the car. Runtime ~2:10–2:30. Radio Voice on the dead-station lines; one Vale on the live lines; never a sweet unison.",
    lyrics: "[Intro — carrier, tuner needle parked]\nThis is not a sign-off.\nThis is a station that already left.\nClosed since ninety-eight.\nYou can still hear the furniture.\n\n[Verse 1 — live line]\nWe walked out arm in arm\nI thought it was you\nThe glass had opinions\nThe parking lot did not\n\n[Harmony — one bar late, last line]\n(we walked out arm in arm)\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nLeave the dial where it died\nDon't hunt for a live one\n\n[Chorus]\nClosed since ninety-eight\nThe ads are for a winter that already thawed\nClosed since ninety-eight\nThird passenger, no body\nIf you sing along you are late\nThat is the arrangement\nClosed since ninety-eight\nWe are both in the wrong seat\n\n[Harmony — one bar late]\n(closed since ninety-eight / the ads are for a winter)\n\n[Verse 2 — live line]\nYour mouth in the rearview\nIs doing last year's sentence\nI keep my hands at ten and two\nLike that will make the faces match\n\n[Harmony — one bar late]\n(your mouth in the rearview)\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nLeave the dial where it died\nDon't hunt for a live one\n\n[Chorus]\nClosed since ninety-eight\nThe ads are for a winter that already thawed\nClosed since ninety-eight\nThird passenger, no body\nIf you sing along you are late\nThat is the arrangement\nClosed since ninety-eight\nWe are both in the wrong seat\n\n[Bridge — Radio Voice only]\nI don't take requests.\nI don't take the present tense.\nIf you needed a song that knows what year it is\nThat is a different carrier.\nWe'll be right back.\nWe were right back.\nWe are still ninety-eight.\n\n[Final Chorus — live line on time, harmony still late]\nClosed since ninety-eight\nDon't correct the reflection\nClosed since ninety-eight\nDon't correct the year\nThe lot is empty except for us\nAnd the us is off by a bar\nClosed since ninety-eight\nKeep driving\n(harmony, one bar later: keep driving)",
    notes: "**What the song is**\nScratchpad seed: two strangers (or The Two) leave a house of mirrors arm in arm with each other’s reflections. Neither notices. The car radio plays a station that closed in 1998. The Radio Voice is the third passenger. Never confirm this is the Continuity Voice.\n\nThe joke is the delay, not the haunting. Nobody says ghost. Nobody says haunted. The year is a filing system.\n\n**Craft (keep this off-mic)**\n- *Static Between Stations* owns leaving the dial **between two live songs**. This is a **dead** station that is still occupying the car.\n- *Quarter to Seventy-Five* owns Ep2 dashboard drift and 3:44. Do not freeze a clock here; freeze a **year**.\n- *Rinse Cycle* owns sign-off. The intro line “this is not a sign-off” is load-bearing — do not let the arrangement become an anthem.\n- *Les Ondes Courtes* owns French-cabaret shortwave costume. Keep this electro-chanson, not accordion.\n- Empty Highway Confession may quote the Radio Voice; this track is the **1998 carpool**, not the 4:17 confession bed (*Whatever Lets Us Be* / *Les Ondes Courtes* still own that scene’s diegetic sing-along unless a later pass retargets).\n\n**Production notes**\n- **Episode placement:** Standalone night-drive musical cutaway; house-of-mirrors exit into a wet lot. EyeWash not required in frame; the radio is enough.\n- **Voice:** Radio Voice (dead-station lines) + one Vale live line. Harmony is always last bar’s lyric.\n- **Structural flaw:** Harmony one bar late for the whole runtime. Final chorus still late.\n- **Runtime target:** 2:10–2:30.",
