    stylePrompt: "Institutional receipt recitation at 80 BPM. Narrow-bandwidth Continuity Voice — warm, tire-ad sincere, never cute, never “dog voice.” Cheap thermal-printer rhythm as percussion (staccato paper advance, not a drum kit). One polite barcode scanner beep that is musically useful and always incomplete. Tape hiss, 60Hz hum, lobby-CRT bed. Dark top end. No guitars. No woof samples. **Structural flaw:** the barcode beep is always one digit short — seven tones instead of eight, every scan, every chorus. The missing digit is Thursday. Do not complete the barcode. Do not let a second beep “finish” it. Mood: a poodle stole the plot and brought back paperwork. Runtime ~1:40–2:00. Use Continuity Voice only on the sung/spoken lead; Biscuit does not sing.",
