    notes: "**What the song is**\nEyeWash Continuity Voice reading **Biscuit’s receipt**. Scratchpad seed: after stealing the plot MacGuffin, Biscuit returns it with a receipt from a store that won’t exist until next Thursday. Comedy stays professionally neutral — this is paperwork, not a cute-dog number.\n\nShips as a Musical cutaway still + motion, **not** gag #9. Do not add it to the eight-gag cycle.\n\n**Craft (keep this off-mic)**\n- *Pepperoni or Margherita* owns Pizza Guy professionalism. This is **station paperwork**, not delivery.\n- *I Second Peggy Babcock* owns HOA hearing tongue-twisters. Do not put Karen on the mic.\n- *Article Seven* owns the skeleton union pause. Biscuit may have been in that yard; this song is the receipt, not the break.\n- Do not score Item Three’s meeting muzak. The gavel may appear as an inventory line only.\n- No barking. No “who’s a good girl.” Continuity Voice does not break character.\n\n**Production notes**\n- **Episode placement:** Biscuit’s Heist (`notes/dialog-jokes-incidents.md`); optional insert near Item Three without replacing that scene’s bed. EyeWash lobby-CRT in frame.\n- **Voice:** Continuity Voice. Biscuit is pictured, not cast as a singer.\n- **Structural flaw:** Barcode beep always one digit short (seven tones, not eight).\n- **Runtime target:** 1:40–2:00.",
