    notes: "**What the song is**\nFake EyeWash sponsor bed for **Ultra-Refreshed Water Lab** — the most refreshing glass of ice water in human history, delivered by an insanely complex window apparatus. Played completely straight. Visual bible: `ideas/ultra-refreshed-water-lab.md`. Prompts already exist: `prompts/ultra-refreshed-water-lab-segments.md`.\n\nThis is **not** a sign-off. The gulp is the hook. The ice is late.\n\n**Craft (keep this off-mic)**\n- *Rinse Cycle* owns fifteen minutes / do not blink / broadcast sign-off. Do not borrow the anthem cadence, the 9-bar phrase, or “do not blink.”\n- *Choose Your Basalt* owns educational cabaret smash-cuts. This is a **sponsor**, not a lesson.\n- *Glam-Sham-Poo / Ultra Screech* owns the joke commercial with a scream. This commercial does not scream. It swallows early.\n- Interior stays dark-top; exterior desk may go clean-digital bright (ice, noon) — same exception family as celestial tracks, but the subject is **glass and sun**, not the sky.\n\n**Production notes**\n- **Episode placement:** `content/cutaways/ultra-refreshed-water-lab.json`. Optional 10s ident loop under other EyeWash sponsor cards (Perpetual Optics adjacent, not a replacement).\n- **Voice:** None sung. Optional Continuity Voice small print only.\n- **Structural flaw:** Gulp one beat before ice hits glass, every pass.\n- **Runtime target:** 1:20–1:40 full; 15–25s core under the existing lab shot.\n- **instrumental:** true. Do not generate a belting vocal if Minimax invents one — prepend `instrumental only, no sung vocal`.",
