    notes: "## Production notes\n- **Episode placement:** The Two cutaway — Episode 1 house-of-mirrors register, but usable anywhere the sisters swap lives (Velvet Rope aftermath, Episode 3 costume change, any dressing room). The town fire stays outside the window.\n- **Emotional arc:** Business-like division of a face → the chorus admits they can't tell either → the bridge is the only time either sister is alone, and she immediately becomes the other → final chorus: the chair is empty and the waltz keeps going.\n- **Characters:** Lillith Vale and Rubella Vale, alternating verses, never on the downbeat together. No third voice. Grok Imagine: both sisters at one vanity, the reflection shows only one of them, never the same one twice.\n- **Structural flaw:** the early/late downbeat is the whole point; do not quantize it. If Minimax locks them together, use the take where it drifts most.\n- **Runtime target:** ~2:45. 15s bumper = intro + first chorus.\n- **Reference energy:** Kurt Weill in a Sephora; Julee Cruise if she had a sister; Tom Waits' waltzes without the gravel.",
